3. |Q|, |R| <= 12: cos, sin of Q*2alpha + R*2beta computed in Q(sqrt5), modulus 1 exactly, floats agree: True
4. (b sqrt2 - d sqrt5)^2 = 2b^2 + 5d^2 - 2bd sqrt10, so bd != 0 would make sqrt10 rational; if d = 0 then b sqrt2 = c forces b = 0. 10 is not a square: True
5. (1 - sqrt-2)^4 = (-7, 4) = -7 + 4 sqrt-2, so e^{2i theta} = (1 - sqrt-2)^2/(1 + sqrt-2)^2: valuation -2 and +2 at the two primes 1 +- sqrt-2 above 3 (3 = (1+sqrt-2)(1-sqrt-2))
   (1 + 2i)^2 = -3 + 4i, so e^{2i alpha} = (1+2i)/(1-2i): valuations +-1 at the primes above 5 only
   |15 e^{2i beta}|^2 = (Fraction(225, 1), Fraction(0, 1)) (= 225): e^{2i beta} lives above 3 and 5 in Q(sqrt5, i)
   Route not used: Q(sqrt-2) and Q(sqrt5, i) have intersection Q (the quadratic subfields of Q(sqrt5, i) are Q(sqrt5), Q(i), Q(sqrt-5)), which the Lean proof uses in the form: sqrt2 is not in Q(sqrt5).
